    {"tenant": "corp.com", "inferred_role": "victim_m365_tenant", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:18:42+0100", "last_seen": "2028-03-15T02:28:42+0100"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts (Cloud)", "technique": "T1078.004", "what_happened": "At 2028-03-15 02:18:42 CEST, Azure AD signinLogs (collected by Wazuh azure-logs module) recorded a Success authentication for global.admin@corp.com from external IP 91.219.236.87. The ClientApp was 'Microsoft Graph API' (direct programmatic API call, NOT the Admin Center web UI). MFA_Result was 'MfaNotRequired' — consistent with a REFRESH TOKEN REPLAY: the attacker obtained an Azure AD refresh token (via prior phishing, stealer log, or token theft on a compromised endpoint) and is now redeeming it against the Graph endpoint, which bypasses the interactive MFA prompt. The source IP 91.219.236.87 is NOT in the global admin's historical baseline (which is admin.corp.com NAT egress + corporate VPN egress).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh Azure decoder on data.azure.signinLogs: TargetUser=global.admin@corp.com + IpAddress=91.219.236.87 + ClientApp=Microsoft Graph API + status=Success + MFA_Result=MfaNotRequired. Composite signature matches refresh-token-replay against a privileged identity from a non-baseline IP.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:18:42+0100"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Detection / Alert Fired", "technique": "T1078.004 (alerting)", "what_happened": "At 02:18:48 CEST (6 seconds after the signin), Wazuh decoder fired an ALERT: 'Global admin signin via Graph API from non-baseline IP without MFA challenge'. The 6-second decoder latency is typical for Azure log ingestion → decode → rule-match pipeline. The alert fired BEFORE any admin action took effect — this was the high-leverage moment for automated session revocation.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh internal decoder pipeline. The rule chains three conditions: privileged account (global.admin tagged Tier-0) + non-baseline IP (geo/IP-history check) + Graph API ClientApp (programmatic, NOT browser). All three together = high-fidelity refresh-token-replay-against-privileged-cloud-account signature.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:18:48+0100"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Impact / Account Manipulation (Disable Victim)", "technique": "T1531", "what_happened": "At 02:22:18 CEST (3 min 36 s after the signin), Azure AD unifiedAuditLog recorded Operation='Update user' against Target=legal.head@corp.com, performed by global.admin@corp.com. The Modified properties field shows AccountEnabled changed from True to False — the attacker DISABLED the legal department head's account. This is operational sabotage: the legal head is the natural escalation contact for ANY suspected breach, and disabling them delays incident notification + regulatory disclosure decisions. Highly diagnostic of intent (not a credential test).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh Azure decoder on data.azure.unifiedAuditLog: Operation=Update user + Target=legal.head@corp.com + Actor=global.admin@corp.com + Modified property=AccountEnabled→false. This action requires global.admin or User.ReadWrite.All scope.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:22:18+0100"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Persistence / Account Manipulation (Rogue Admin)", "technique": "T1098.003", "what_happened": "At 02:22:42 CEST (24 s after disabling legal head), Operation='Add member to role' fired in unifiedAuditLog: Target=attacker.shadow@corp.com (an attacker-controlled account, name strongly suggestive of recently-created or recently-discovered shadow identity), Role='Global Administrator'. The attacker created a SECOND Global Administrator account inside the tenant — this is the playbook PB81 textbook 'rogue admin' persistence technique. Even if global.admin's credentials are eventually rotated, attacker.shadow remains a valid Tier-0 identity controlled by the attacker.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh Azure decoder on data.azure.unifiedAuditLog: Operation=Add member to role + Target=attacker.shadow@corp.com + Role=Global Administrator + Actor=global.admin@corp.com. The 24-second gap from the previous admin action confirms scripted execution.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:22:42+0100"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Exfiltration / Mailbox Export", "technique": "T1567.002 + T1114.002", "what_happened": "At 02:24:18 CEST, Operation='New-MailboxExportRequest' fired in unifiedAuditLog: Target=ceo@corp.com (the CEO mailbox), Destination='https://attacker-relay.cloud/exports/' (external attacker-controlled URL), ExportLargeFolder=True (exports the ENTIRE mailbox including large folders). This is a BULK MAILBOX EXPORT to an external attacker URL — the CEO's email history (board communications, M&A plans, financials, credentials shared via email) is being staged for exfiltration to the attacker. T1567.002 (Exfiltration to Cloud Storage) + T1114.002 (Email Collection: Remote Email Collection) combined.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh Azure decoder on data.azure.unifiedAuditLog: Operation=New-MailboxExportRequest + Target=ceo@corp.com + Destination URL outside tenant boundary + ExportLargeFolder=True. The destination URL is the highest-fidelity exfiltration indicator — legitimate mailbox exports go to internal Exchange Online or audited mailbox archives, never to external arbitrary URLs.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:24:18+0100"},
    {"step": 6, "tactic": "Defense Evasion / Disable Logging", "technique": "T1562.008", "what_happened": "At 02:28:42 CEST (~6 minutes after the signin, ~4 minutes after the mailbox export request), Operation='Set-OrganizationConfig' fired: Property=AuditDisabled changed to True. The attacker DISABLED tenant-wide audit logging — this is anti-forensics: any further actions performed by global.admin or attacker.shadow after this moment will NOT generate unifiedAuditLog entries. The 6-minute action window before audit-off is the only forensic-visible portion of the attack; everything after 02:28:42 is forensic-blind unless tenant audit is re-enabled.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh Azure decoder on data.azure.unifiedAuditLog: Operation=Set-OrganizationConfig + Property=AuditDisabled + new value=True + Actor=global.admin@corp.com. The action is performed LAST in the chain — classic defense-evasion-after-objectives-completed sequencing.", "first_seen": "2028-03-15T02:28:42+0100"}
  ],
